CC   IMGT/LIGM-DB annotation level: by annotators
CC   
CC   The germline sequence in [2] is derived by combining the germline
CC   5' flanking sequence with the rearranged C-region sequence. The
CC   sequence in [2] and [3] differs from the germline sequence [1] at
CC   13 positions, all of which are in the flanking or intron regions
CC   except one (base 2774), which changes the deduced amino acid at
CC   that position from Trp to Leu. The authors state that this is
CC   consistent with the amino acid sequence of the myeloma protein.
CC   Also reported [2] is a rearranged pseudogene epsilon-3. [1] reports
CC   a germline pseudogene epsilon-2 and the alpha-1 and alpha-2 genes.
CC   [3] reports the epsilon-2 gene.
CC   This entry is part of a multigene region (region B), which includes
CC   the gamma-2, gamma-4, epsilon-1, and alpha-2 genes. See segment 1
CC   for more comments.
CC   Complete source information:
CC   Human placenta DNA [1], clone 38A; 5' flank -- fetal liver DNA
CC   library (clone CH4A-H-Ig-epsilon-12) [2], C-region -- myeloma cell
CC   line 266b1 (clone CH4A-H-Ig-epsilon-11) [2]; fetal liver DNA,
CC   library of T. Maniatis [3].
